Z||000000||bHooper||05-31-2001||07:10 PM||||so, remember the "old thing" about getting more cash for a crushed fiero?  guess what?  it's true!<P>i have spent the past two days at this salvage yard, working on 2 cars that are going to crush on monday.  today, i asked the attendant (John) about the "silly little rumor" that GM paid money for titles of crushed fiero's.  John said, that that was absolutely true!  he said that a few years back, they had 15 fiero's (10 of which cranked) and the boss told him to put them to the crusher when it came.  after they were crushed, the "crusher man" told John that he would get <B>twice as much money</B> for the trailer load of fiero's as he would for all the other cars that were crushed!  apparently, when a fiero is crushed, it doesn't go to the normal "scrap yard", it get's hauled off to some special place!<P>he also said that his boss refuses to buy fiero's anymore, even though he can get them for like $80 at the auctions!<P>anyway, whenever you see a car at the salvage yard, you need to strip <B>all</B> the useable parts off of it, cause it aint gonna be there too long!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
