Z||000005||Fformula88||05-31-2001||09:15 PM||||Sounds like a big load of it to me!  I know GM killed it, but I would really doubt they are out to totally eliminate it from the planet.  After all, they give it some attention in their Pontiac 75th Anniversary stuff.  Maybe a crushed Fiero is worth some $$, but its got a lot of steel in that space frame too.  Maybe a junked Fiero has more useable (not rusted out) metal left on it than say a Cavalier.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||09:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Maybe a crushed Fiero is worth some $$, but its got a lot of steel in that space frame too.  Maybe a junked Fiero has more useable (not rusted out) metal left on it than say a Cavalier.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That sounds like a better explanation.  Unless they have some sort of gripe against us who are trying to preserve our Fieros....a conspiracy?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
